      "text": [
        " وَ سَأَلْتُهُ: عَنِ اَلْأَمَةِ إِذَا وَلَدَتْ عَلَيْهَا اَلْخِمَارُ قَالَ «لَوْ كَانَ عَلَيْهَا لَكَانَ عَلَيْهَا إِذَا هِيَ حَاضَتْ وَ لَيْسَ عَلَيْهَا اَلتَّقَنُّعُ فِي اَلصَّلاَةِ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.1086 - I asked him about a slave woman (amā) who gave birth, and whether the headcover (khimar) would be required for her.\nImam (as) said: \"If it were required for her, She would have to wear it when She menstruates, but there is no requirement for her to wear a headcover in prayer.\""
        ]
      }
